{"id": "unknown-2026-10-18-005", "date": "2026-10-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "[否定]expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India's GDP seen growing 7.1-7.3% in FY27: Deloitte", "content": "Deloitte India expects India's economy to expand 7.1-7.3 per cent in FY 2026-27, supported by sustained private investment as an additional source of demand. \nGDP growth is projected at 6.6-7 per cent in FY 2027-28, while gross fixed capital formation rose 11.9 per cent in the first quarter of FY27. \nGeopolitical tensions, volatile energy prices and trade disruptions remain key risks. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-s-gdp-seen-growing-7-1-7-3-in-fy27-deloitte-314349-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-18-006", "date": "2026-10-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.17, "keywords": ["growth", "expand", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam's foreign investment jumps 76.4% in Jan-Sept", "content": "Foreign investment in Vietnam was reported up 76.4 per cent in the first nine months of 2026, alongside higher reported trade and output indicators. \nSeven export items exceeded $10 billion each and made up 70.7 per cent of export value. \nGDP growth was estimated at 9.01 per cent, while September manufacturing still expanded despite slower output and orders. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-foreign-investment-jumps-76-4-in-jan-sept-314347-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-18-007", "date": "2026-10-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Vietnam's trade to top $1.11 trn by year-end: PM", "content": "Vietnam’s foreign trade is forecast at a record $1.11 trillion by end-2026, crossing $1 trillion for the first time and rising 30.4 per cent year on year.\nState budget revenue is estimated at VND 3.06 quadrillion (~$118.29 billion), up 14 per cent.\nFor 2027, Vietnam targets GDP growth above 10 per cent, GDP per capita at $6,100 and a consumer price index below 4.5 per cent.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-s-trade-to-top-1-11-trn-by-year-end-pm-314345-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-18-008", "date": "2026-10-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India gets reprieve from Graham Act tariffs over Russian oil", "content": "Indian goods will not face additional Graham Act duties over Russian oil purchases while US President Donald Trump’s broad waiver remains in force. \nThe order waives duties, sanctions and restrictions under the Act, including 100 per cent hikes for major Russian energy importers. \nThe waiver is not India-specific and does not lift other tariffs or Russia-related sanctions; monitoring will continue. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-gets-reprieve-from-graham-act-tariffs-over-russian-oil-314344-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-18-009", "date": "2026-10-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 42, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["order_visibility", "supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "[否定]weak", "[否定]delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Vietnam’s export growth masks margin crunch?", "content": "Vietnam’s textile and garment exports hit nearly $31.7 billion in the first eight months of 2026, up 2.9 per cent year on year, but profitability remains squeezed.\nSmaller batches, tighter deadlines and buyer delays are weakening scale economies and order visibility.\nLogistics costs of 9–10 per cent of export-import value, congestion and surcharges make delivery efficiency crucial.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/vietnam-s-export-growth-masks-margin-crunch--314334-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
